    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestions!\r\n\r\n- 'AckslD/nvim-neoclip.lua': there is a functionality in 'mini.bracketed' which solves the main problem that 'nvim-neoclip.lua' aims to solve. That is, \"remembering\" yank history and allowing inserting from it. This is solved by [\"yank\" target](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/848c5e8f428faf843051768e0d56104cd02aea1f/doc/mini-bracketed.txt#L530). Example: after pressing `p` to put text, navigate through yank history with `[y`, `]y`.\r\n- 'Zeioth/garbage-day.nvim': it *might* be a feature of some possible 'mini.lsp', but I don't really see it being part of 'mini.nvim' in any foreseeable future.\r\n- 'petertriho/nvim-scrollbar' - there is a [pure scrollbar config in 'mini.map'](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/848c5e8f428faf843051768e0d56104cd02aea1f/doc/mini-map.txt#L357-L382). You can check the differences with that plugin [here](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/848c5e8f428faf843051768e0d56104cd02aea1f/doc/mini-map.txt#L118-L123).\r\n\r\nClosing as there is either already a solution present or probably will never happen.",
            "created_at": "2024-09-30T08:12:17Z",
